                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>How is Chennai's jewelry market different from Mumbai + Delhi + Bengaluru?</h3>
                                        <p>T Nagar + Panagal Park is India's densest jewelry-retail concentration (300+ stores in 2 km). South India buyer prefers 22-24k gold + temple + antique + South Indian heritage designs. Festive + Akshaya Tritiya + Onam + Diwali seasonality. Family + gifting-driven purchase with high trust threshold.</p>
                                        <h3>What makes Kolkata + Bengali jewelry marketing distinct?</h3>
                                        <p>Bengali bridal jewelry is a distinct sub-vertical (conch-shell bangles, iron-bangle, gold-plating traditions, Bengali wedding-specific sets). Bowbazar + Barabazar wholesale corridors. Durga Puja + Poila Boishakh + Bengali wedding season peaks. Bengali + English + Hindi creative needs.</p>
                                        <h3>Do we need Tamil + Malayalam + Bengali language creative for Chennai + Kolkata jewelry brands?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes for regional catchment + festive + wedding-season campaigns. Native-speaker creative + culturally-accurate messaging outperforms English-only by 25-40% on cost + engagement. English-only works only if targeting pure urban + high-income + young-professional segments.</p>
                                        <h3>What is a realistic agency retainer for Chennai + Kolkata jewelry brands?</h3>
                                        <p>Same tiered pricing as pan-India: Rs 65K-Rs 1.5 lakh Starter, Rs 1.5-3.5 lakh Growth, Rs 4 lakh+ Enterprise. Regional-language creative production may add 5-10% to standard pricing due to specialised writer + editor contracts. Ad spend separate.</p>
                                        <h3>Does ITD handle regional-language creative production?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes. Native-speaker Tamil, Malayalam, Bengali writers + editors + video captioners on contract for regional-language creative production. Culturally-accurate messaging reviewed by regional strategists. Multilingual A/B testing on paid channels to validate creative-language fit.</p>
                                        <h3>How does ITD support broader South + East India catchment strategy?</h3>
                                        <p>Chennai-based brand: Tamil Nadu + Kerala + Karnataka + Andhra + Telangana catchment via regional-language creative + geo-targeting + regional festive-calendar planning + regional-language WhatsApp funnels. Kolkata-based brand: West Bengal + Odisha + Assam + Jharkhand catchment via Bengali + Odia + Assamese where volume justifies + regional festive planning.</p>
                                        <h3>Are temple jewelry + antique-heritage sub-verticals worth building around?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes for Chennai + Kolkata brands. Distinct sub-verticals with strong regional demand + limited D2C competition + strong festive + bridal + gifting economics. Requires heritage-authentic brand narrative + expert design + traditional-craft partnerships + certification + provenance transparency.</p>
